    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear what you're saying, but it feels like you're kind of brushing off the other side. If someone believes that biological sex is the only objective metric and that using gender identity to define people is actually unscientific or even harmful to how we classify humans, isn't that a legitimate scientific debate? Or is the scientific community basically saying those views are just wrong?",
